  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "column: free custom fields on invalid occurrence to prevent leak",
  "description": "Summary:\n\nIn parse_column_format(), col_custom_fields is dynamically allocated using g_strdup() when cust_format_info-\\>len \\> 0. If parsing the subsequent occurrence token fails (e.g. an invalid numeric string such as \"abc\" or trailing non-numeric characters), the function frees fmt_copy and unreferences cust_format_info, but returns false without freeing col_custom_fields.\n\nThis causes a persistent heap memory leak (CWE-401) whenever a malformed custom column format is parsed from configuration files or CLI options.\n\nChanges:\n\n\\- Added g_free(col_custom_fields) before returning false on occurrence parsing error.\n\n\\- Verified with tools/check_apis.py (0 warnings).\n\n\\- Pre-tested under GCC with -Wall -Wextra -Werror -Wsign-compare (0 warnings, 0 errors).\n\n\\- Validated with unit test harness confirming zero leaked allocations on error paths.",
